{{see also|Texas's 26th congressional district}}
The 26th district is based in the northern portion of the [[Dallas–Fort Worth metroplex]], centering on eastern [[Denton County, Texas|Denton County]] and including [[Cooke County, Texas|Cooke County]], part of [[Wise County, Texas|Wise County]] and a very small portion of [[Tarrant County, Texas|Tarrant County]]. The incumbent was Republican [[Michael C. Burgess|Michael Burgess]], who was re-elected with 69.29% of the vote in 2022 against a [[Libertarian Party (US)|Libertarian]] candidate.<ref name="HPVT"/> Burgess chose to retire.

