{{See also|Texas's 28th congressional district}}
The 28th district is based in the [[Laredo, Texas|Laredo]] area and stretches north of the [[Rio Grande Valley (Texas)|Rio Grande Valley]] into east [[San Antonio]]. The incumbent was Democrat [[Henry Cuellar]], who was re-elected with 56.65% of the vote in 2022.<ref name="HPVT"/> 
<!--
On June 3, 2024, the National Republican Congressional Committee added Cuellar to its list of Democratic members to aim to defeat in November. <ref>https://www.texastribune.org/2024/06/03/republican-cuellar-investment/</ref>

In early June 2024, Judge Lee Rosenthal granted a request from Cuellar's Defense and the Prosecution to delay the trial. The jury selection will begin on March 31st, 2025. <ref>https://www.msn.com/en-us/news/politics/texas-rep-henry-cuellar-s-federal-corruption-trial-delayed-until-2025/ar-BB1nS9q3?ocid=BingNewsSearch</ref>
-->

