{{see also|Texas's 33rd congressional district}}
The 33rd district is in the [[Dallas–Fort Worth metroplex]], encompassing [[Downtown Fort Worth]], western [[Dallas, Texas|Dallas]], and parts of [[Grand Prairie, Texas|Grand Prairie]], [[Irving, Texas|Irving]], [[Carrollton, Texas|Carrollton]], and [[Farmers Branch, Texas|Farmers Branch]]. The incumbent was Democrat [[Marc Veasey]], who was re-elected with 71.98% of the vote in 2022.<ref name="HPVT"/>

